<Layout title="Exploring journal-based CDC for InterSystems IRIS" description="A technical perspective on journal-based change data capture for InterSystems IRIS and Kafka."><section class="page-hero"><div class="container"><a class="back-link" href={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}insights/`}>← Back to insights</a><span class="eyebrow">ARCHITECTURE / RESEARCH</span><h1>Exploring journal-based CDC for InterSystems IRIS</h1><p class="lede">What changes when data capture starts at the transaction journal rather than at the application layer?</p></div></section><section class="content-section"><div class="container rich-text"><p>InterSystems IRIS often sits at the centre of operational workflows, while downstream systems need updates in near real time. The integration challenge is not simply moving data: it is capturing meaningful changes without introducing excessive application coupling or database load.</p><h2>Why investigate the journal?</h2><p>Application hooks, scheduled exports and polling approaches can be effective, but they also introduce design trade-offs. A journal-oriented approach explores a lower-level source of changes that may reduce the need to instrument each application path.</p><h2>The difficult parts</h2><p>Decoding physical journal changes is not equivalent to publishing clean business events. A practical pipeline must handle transaction boundaries, record formats, data mappings, recovery, replay, security and downstream compatibility. Exactly-once effects require careful end-to-end design rather than a label on the transport.</p><h2>Our direction</h2><p>We are prototyping a CDC pipeline that interprets relevant IRIS journal changes and publishes structured change events to Kafka. The architecture is exploratory; publicly documented benchmarks, compatibility details and production guarantees will be provided only when validated.</p><div class="notice">Interested in evaluating this approach in a controlled environment? We are looking for design partners who can share real integration requirements.</div><p><a class="button button-primary" href={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}products/iris-cdc/#early-access`}>Explore early access ↗</a></p></div></section></Layout>
